---------- Forwarded message ----------
From: Daniel Swislow <dswislow at ndi.org>
Date: Thu, Aug 9, 2012 at 12:51 AM
Subject: Including Finnish organization logos with the Declaration on
Parliamentary Openness
To: juha.yrjola at gmail.com, Leo Lahti <leo.lahti at iki.fi>


Juha and Leo,

Hope all is well since Paris. We're looking forward to participating at OKF
in Helsinki in the coming weeks -- hopefully we'll get to see each other
again.

I just wanted to write you a quick note about the Declaration on
Parliamentary Openness, which we talked about at the conference in Paris.
We are currently collecting logos of organizations that either participated
in the development of the document or would like to indicate their support
for the principles within it. I noticed we don't have any organizations
from Finland yet included. If you're interested, check out the Declaration
at www.openingparliament.org/declaration and the listing of current
supporters (which is in progress) at www.openingparliament.org/organizations.
We'd love to include your organizations from Finland. The logos will be
listed on the website and included with the published version of the
document, which will be officially launched on September 15 in Rome on the
International Day of Democracy at the World e-Parliament Conference 2012.

Also, I know Leo is already in the group, but I wasn't sure about you,
Juha. There is a large Google group (I know, not another one!) of PMOs
around the world. About 150 members representing 50 countries are currently
members, and we'd love for you to join if you haven't already. The link is
here: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/pmo-network

Thanks to you both!

Dan

